cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Quiver in research, please cite it as below."
title: "Quiver: dependency-free C++23 analytical kernels with runtime SIMD dispatch"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Moustafa Nasr"
    alias: "div0rce"
repository-code: "https://github.com/div0rce/quiver"
url: "https://div0rce.github.io/quiver/"
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.7.0
date-released: 2026-07-11
keywords:
  - simd
  - vectorized-execution
  - analytical-kernels
  - columnar
  - avx2
  - avx512
  - neon
  - cpp23
abstract: >-
  A dependency-free C++23 library of ten vectorized analytical kernel families (compare, filter,
  selection conversion, mask algebra, take/dictionary decode, reduce, hash, bit-unpack, arithmetic,
  guarded arithmetic) behind runtime scalar/AVX2/AVX-512/NEON dispatch, with a reproducible
  cross-ISA performance ledger whose methodology deletes noisy results instead of publishing them.
